{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers","id":1519182,"title":"Have you ever spent the day just creating new amalgam powers or disciplines powers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-30T10:30:24-07:00","id":1519182,"title":"Have you ever spent the day just creating new amalgam powers or disciplines powers?","content":"I find that I do it fairly often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T12:37:49-07:00","id":1519195,"title":"","content":"Yes... the results are in Player's Guide to the Low Clans and Player's Guide to High Clans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T13:28:40-07:00","id":1519197,"title":"","content":"I find it quite fun and sometimes hard to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T13:59:38-07:00","id":1519201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers#post1519182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that I do it fairly often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told i spend more time retooling Elder powers that i find subpar into amalgam powers.<br /> Ditto for a number of signature disciplines of the Independents, Sabbat clans and bloodlines.\u200b<br /> <br /> Things get loopy enough with a variety of them, occult [no thaumaturgy requirement] rituals and a few supernatural merits &amp; flaws tweaked into backgrounds, loresheets and such.<br /> <br /> Specially when you also add one's own bits of cryptolore/metaplot, like having 4+ different groups of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nagaraja_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">flesh-eating necromancers</a>, each prevalent <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493721-bloodlines-the-best-and-the-worst?p=1494195#post1494195\">in a different part of the world</a>, claiming a different origin of its own and none named anything remotely similar to Nagaraja, among other &quot;what was that bloodline's canon origin anyway? i forget...&quot; shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T16:55:49-07:00","id":1519206,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been reworking some of the more advanced discipline powers into amalgam powers such as Soulmask into something that my Malkavian player would want to learn to present himself as something more harmless or appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T17:24:29-07:00","id":1519210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1519206#post1519206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve been reworking some of the more advanced discipline powers into amalgam powers such as Soulmask into something that my Malkavian player would want to learn to present himself as something more harmless or appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, have this then:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mask the Ephemeral (Auspex 2-4, Obfuscate 3)<br /> With awareness of the invisible world, comes an awareness of deeper layers of obfuscation and invisibility.<br /> <br /> (An amalgam to cover the niche of &quot;Auspex-countering effects&quot; filled by powers such as Mind Blank &amp; Soul Mask. Auspex 2 for aura-tweaking, Auspex 4 for false thoughts, higher level Obfuscate variants might allow for not just hiding one's aura or thoughts, but the creation of false one's according to the user preference much like with a false visage) </div> </div> </div>Might as well get that conceptual ball rolling.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T07:35:11-07:00","id":1519248,"title":"","content":"I occasional trick ill do is replicate powers with discipline Combo for example I homebrewed an agg damage shadow blade with Pot 2 ob2.<br /> <br /> since were talking powers<br /> <br /> Vissitude 3 auspex 4-the targets is shaped to the form of their deepest desires.<br /> <br /> Protean 4 mortis 3- the bones of the ancient dead erupt from the ground. Occult+perception diff 6 each success scores 2 lethal damage can be dodged in diff 8.<br /> <br /> Vissitude 3 Dominate 3/vaulderie ritual-person is turned into a completly differant person during their embrace number of success reflects level of change from a simular person to completely differant outlooks, genders, ethnicity etc. How much subject retains of previous self in terms of memory is relative to willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T09:23:43-07:00","id":1519259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers#post1519182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that I do it fairly often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty, lately. Especially for my 7th gen Warrior of Glycon from VDA20.<br /> <br /> Current favourites:<br /> <br /> <b>Potence 6</b><br /> <i>Sculptor of the Heavens: </i>grants automatic successes on sculpting and building rolls involving hard materials, using your supernatural strength to manipulate them with great ease. It's inspired and mirrrors a Celerity 6 power, Precision, which gives automatic successes on creative rolls which benefit from great precision. The idea is to allow my character - otherwise a warrior with no dots in Crafts at the moment - to produce statues, build temples and inscribe hyeroglyphs in the rock to glorify Set. What he lacks for in skill - which he could pick up on with time anyway - he makes up by being able to manipulate stone like butter and using huge blocks for buildings.<br /> <br /> <b>Obfuscate 6</b><br /> <i>Taken by the Duat: </i>make people disappear with you when you do a successful hold on them. If you were already invisible and succeed in the hold, they suddenly vanish from sight without you breaking your Obfuscate. The victims stay invisible until they manage to escape your hold. Sounds they might make are not an issue because in this edition Obfuscate 1 does the sphere of silence that used to be Quietus 1.<br /> <i>Crocodile Strike: </i>still need to write it in detail, and it might end up being merged somehow with <i>Taken by the Duat</i>, but the idea is to make it easier or automatic not to break the concealment given by Obfuscate 2 when you do sneak attacks. In this edition sneak attacks are already possible with Obfuscate 2 and you can avoid breaking the concealment with a Wits + Stealth roll (difficulty and number of successes required are determined by the Storyteller), but this power aims at making sneak attacks super easy without needing to reactivate Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> <b>Serpentis 6</b><br /> I wrote a lot of powers for Serpentis drawing inspiration from Greek and Egyptian mythology. These are only some of my favourites:<br /> <i>Bite of Ammit: </i>upgrade the Typhonic Maw (Serpentis 2) to be able to drink 1 blood point per damage inflicted when attacking with the tongue or bite, and if you kill an enemy with the tongue or bite you can diablerise him automatically.<br /> <i>Typhon's Wings</i>: Typhon is depicted with wings sometimes, so you basically get wings, 2 free dots in Flight and keep Flight as an in-clan discipline (basically the same as a Daimoinon 6 power) when you activate Typhonic Avatar (Serpentis 4).<br /> <i>Skin of Mehen / Helios' Dracos: </i>Mehen is an Egyptian snake that guards the boat of Ra; one Greek myth says the chariot of Helios is carried by winged snakes. It upgrades Skin of the Serpent (Serpentis 3) to protect against fire and sun damage like it does from other damage (normally it works against all damage except sun and fire).<br /> <i>Amphinekros: </i>the name means &quot;dead in both&quot; like amphibios (&gt;amphibian) means &quot;living in both&quot;. It's based on the link between snakes and different realms of existence, especially life and death, but also demons and jinn. I'm still working on it, as it started as a power to travel through the Underworld, then I thought instead of making it something to perceive and attack spirits, ghosts and demons (like the sorcerers' Quietus 4 from V20's Lore of the Clans), and the last idea has been a way to use the forked tongue and snake's great smell to sense nearby supernaturals and get detailed info on them, not only for the immaterial ones (spirit, ghosts, demons), but also vampires, lupines, etc. Depending on the successes on the activation roll, it should tell me not only direction, distance and type of supernatural creatures nearby, but also their clan or tribe and possibly generation (for vampires) and age (for lupines). It's still work in progress to make sure it's not overpowered, but it mostly does things other powers in some disciplines do at a lower level, but combining them or making it easier to activate or giving more accurate results. If I stick with the idea of it being smell-based, the name is probably going to change to something like <i>Ophidian Smell </i>or <i>Scent of the Stranger</i> (i.e. the supernatural). The ability to attack immaterial beings will be based on using the body parts transformed by Serpentis, not the whole body or weapons, so it's really the snake-ness of the character that allows it to act across the Gauntlet / Shroud. Also, it specifically does not pierce Obfuscate because the latter is a mind control power at the end of the day which makes you ignore the presence of the obfuscated character, so even if my smell picks up the scent of an obfuscated vampire, he will simply ignore it.<br /> <br /> EDIT, or rather, UPDATE: I figured the ability to smell supernaturals should be a combo between Auspex 2 and Serpentis 2, while the ability to strike immaterial beings should be a Serpentis 6 power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 07-31-2023, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T12:38:37-07:00","id":1519277,"title":"","content":"Variation on nephandi rote I came up with<br /> <br /> &quot;You touch my mind, fumbling in ignorance.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dominanion/dark thaumaturgy 3 presence 3 (paths only)<br /> <br /> a defence against telepathic attacks such as auspex probes and dominate. The using spends a willpower point flexively and rolls their path rating (diff target willpower) to make direct psychic contract with 'patrons mind acting as a sort of conduct between her attacker. Such sanity blasting experiances cause the victim to blackout, drain a point of willpower point per success on the victim and a derangement for every 3 success, either the flaw the flaw nightmares or a derangement.A botch results in loss of permanent willpower and path level as their soul is shredded while the attacked gain a permanent dot of courage having stood firm in the face of the crawling chaos....and typically a fierce contempt for the infernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-31-2023, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T09:29:46-07:00","id":1519449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1519210#post1519210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, have this then:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Might as well get that conceptual ball rolling.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for some of your hard work Baaldam and I wasn't expecting that type of response at all or from the other posters in general who took the time to show some of there work on some of there homebrewed powers. For some reason I wasn't expecting such details on some of the posts I got.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T14:03:42-07:00","id":1520548,"title":"","content":"Interesting enough many of the amalgam powers are becoming clan specific, which in my case is the Malkavian clan and nothing for the Brujah or Gangrel clans themselves. Have you fallen into same pattern yourself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T14:59:26-07:00","id":1520550,"title":"","content":"I tend to rework disciplines and paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T15:02:33-07:00","id":1520713,"title":"","content":"How does the reworking of paths work out for you Hello? It's an enjoyable struggle to create Amalgam powers based on high level elder disciplines and figuring out how to work it out on paper or why so and so would know it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T20:08:43-07:00","id":1520739,"title":"","content":"No, but I have used Disciplines to emulate the powers of other non-vampire NPC's.<br /> <br /> No joke, I've written up stats for quite a few iconic characters in a WoD game using VTM's Disciplines and Numina such as Freddy Krueger, Jason Voorhees, Michael Myers, Carrie White, Tommy Jarvis, Nancy Thompson, Samuel Loomis, and Creighton Duke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T15:38:48-07:00","id":1520841,"title":"","content":"Neat idea Matt and how did the idea work out in your games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T23:27:16-07:00","id":1520923,"title":"","content":"Reading this thread I am wondering if I should make &quot;Soul Mastery&quot; go from a set of devotion powers to a Disicipline in itself? But those are just some loose thoughts for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T05:13:56-07:00","id":1520935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers#post1519182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that I do it fairly often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Level 4 and 6 Powers are the msot interesting and curious for me to think about. They seem to be the level tilted towards practicality, immiediate results and accomplishing objectives, and interesting and new developments, concepts, and ideas. It does seem that each Discipline does have level ( or magnitude ) 6 powers and abilities that are certainly can give long term and relatively risk free results and advantages. <br /> <br /> My favourite Disciplines are definitely : Presence, Protean, Dominate, Auspex, Celerity, Fortitude. Of course other - like Obfuscate and Necromancy - are also worthy of consideration and attention, and clearly well written and described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T10:53:28-07:00","id":1520960,"title":"","content":"I find that I do lots of amalgam powers based off of level 6 disciplines for many of the same reasons you do Muad'Dib and my favorite Disciplines as you know from the favorite Discipline post is Presence, Obfuscate, Protean and Fortitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T03:56:44-07:00","id":1521117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1520960#post1520960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that I do lots of amalgam powers based off of level 6 disciplines for many of the same reasons you do Muad'Dib and my favorite Disciplines as you know from the favorite Discipline post is Presence, Obfuscate, Protean and Fortitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, is Protean considered a normal or common Discipline, or is in similar to Serpentis or Obtenebration in regard to this matter ?<br /> <br /> I've searched on this topic before, but only Vampire: Dark Ages had paragraphs that came close. <br /> Are there any alternative terms, names, and words to refer to particular Disciplines ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T08:04:56-07:00","id":1521131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1520841#post1520841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat idea Matt and how did the idea work out in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worked very well in the case of both Jason Voorhees and Freddy Krueger. <br /> <br /> I had it to where Freddy's razor glove did aggravated damage in the Dream World (and by extension, the Umbra and the Dreaming) but only did lethal damage in the real world. <br /> <br /> With Jason, I gave him Potence 5, Celerity 5, Fortitude 5, Obfuscate 2, and Auspex 2 and had all his Physical attributes at 5, his Social attributes all at 0, and his Mental attributes all at 2. He was able to send a Brujah PC into torpor but our Tremere and our Toreador were able to finish him off via a mix of guns and Lure of Flames for good measure. The Brujah did soften up Jason a lot in the combat encounter though and Jason was tough enough to leave the surviving PC's mauled pretty badly.<br /> <br /> I might post the character sheets soon enough","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T09:28:06-07:00","id":1521132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1521117#post1521117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, is Protean considered a normal or common Discipline, or is in similar to Serpentis or Obtenebration in regard to this matter ?<br /> <br /> I've searched on this topic before, but only Vampire: Dark Ages had paragraphs that came close.<br /> Are there any alternative terms, names, and words to refer to particular Disciplines ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it I would view along the lines as Serpentis or Tzimisce or the Ravnos or Lasombra Discipline as not a common/normal discipline in my viewpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T09:30:14-07:00","id":1521133,"title":"","content":"Jason might not be the sharpest knife in the drawer, but when you can survive anything and single minded as he is is that perhaps having brains might be a weakness for him and he would feel fear and do something unexpected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T13:42:47-07:00","id":1521147,"title":"","content":"Though I'm not sure what you class Michael Meyers as he is for intents and purposes a regular human with seemingly no supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-21-2023, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T01:24:37-07:00","id":1521166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1521132#post1521132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it I would view along the lines as Serpentis or Tzimisce or the Ravnos or Lasombra Discipline as not a common/normal discipline in my viewpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do recall Protean being called secret or specialtiy of the Gangrel Vampires. Since ancient eras various Kindred have approach Gangrel Vampires for tutelage and knowledge of these Powers.<br /> <br /> However I have to mention that Protean was introduced early enough and the Discipline appears and is discussed more often than for example Obtenebration, as far as I know. When reading various books I often had the idea and impression that Protean was as common or available as for example as Celerity or Dominate. This impression was especially noteworthy early in my introduction to VtM books and supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T11:56:19-07:00","id":1521210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1521147#post1521147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I'm not sure what you class Michael Meyers as he is for intents and purposes a regular human with seemingly no supernatural powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never wrote stats for Michael Myers but if I did, he'd just be a min-maxed mortal who's really good at combat and stealth<br /> <br /> Like he'd have Stealth and Melee at 5 and maybe a 1 in Security or Larceny.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, here's my write-up for Freddy Krueger in VTM. Again, I'm using the 2e rules and not V5, with Disciplines to simulate his powers. Instead of vitae, he's got Pathos to fuel his powers but it's functionally the same as using a blood pool. He refills it by spreading fear or by killing or injuring others in the Dream World.<br /> <br /> <b>Freddy Krueger</b><br /> <br /> Clan: Dream Demon (if we're using Wraith terms, he's a Sandman and a Risen)<br /> Nature: Sadist<br /> Demeanor: Jester<br /> <br /> Strength: 4/Dexterity: 4/Stamina: 4<br /> Charisma: 3/Manipulation: 3/Appearance: 0<br /> Perception: 5/Intelligence: 3/Wits: 5<br /> <br /> Path Rating: Humanity 0<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Pathos Pool: 15<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Chimestry 5, Obfuscate 4, Auspex 5, Celerity 4, Fortitude 5, Potence 4, Presence 1, Dominate 5, Quietus 1, Animalism 2, Dementation 3, Vicissitude 4, Necromancy 5, Thaumaturgy 5 (Lure of Flames 4, Path of Conjuring 3, Movement of the Mind 5, Spirit Thaumaturgy 2, Path of Blood 1)<br /> <br /> Abilities: Intimidation 5, Brawl 4, Dodge 5, Alertness 5, Acting 3, Athletics 3, Empathy 5, Subterfuge 5, Animal Ken 3, Drive 2, Etiquette 1, Firearms 2, Melee 5, Repair 4, Music 1, Security 4, Stealth 5, Occult 5, Investigation 3, Law 1, Science 1<br /> <br /> Equipment: Razor Glove (Strength + 2)<br /> <br /> He's got two different forms. In the Dream World, he has the classic grubby hobo look from Part 1, while in the Real World, he dons the heavy black trenchcoat, turtleneck sweater, and leather pants from New Nightmare (AKA Part 7).<br /> <br /> The only real difference between the two forms is that the Real World Freddy's glove does Lethal Damage (it does Aggravated Damage in the Dream World) but his trenchcoat, thicker sweater, and heavy leather pants act as light armor (he gets one extra dice to soak damage in that form)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T14:18:45-07:00","id":1521221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1521166#post1521166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do recall Protean being called secret or specialtiy of the Gangrel Vampires. Since ancient eras various Kindred have approach Gangrel Vampires for tutelage and knowledge of these Powers.<br /> <br /> However I have to mention that Protean was introduced early enough and the Discipline appears and is discussed more often than for example Obtenebration, as far as I know. When reading various books I often had the idea and impression that Protean was as common or available as for example as Celerity or Dominate. This impression was especially noteworthy early in my introduction to VtM books and supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always viewed Protean as a specialist discipline that not every Kindred can learn easily as it requires the right degree of mental flexibilty I guess and why I never classed it as a &quot;common&quot; power among the undead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-22-2023, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T09:43:25-07:00","id":1521671,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Yeah! I'm currently working on converting my Requiem game/setting in V5 after we took a long break. I like V5 base mechanics but I vastly prefer Requiem's approach to vampirism, thus I'm reworking Requiem's five clan discipline. For most disciplines I can simply take their v5 equivalent, but for Majesty and Nightmare, I have to get a bit creative.<br /> <br /> For Majesty I mostly shuffled powers around, added a power to cause compulsions, or a higher-level power to boost Entrancement (which I reduced to a 2nd-level power).<br /> <br /> For Nightmare I've had to create new powers and convert requiem ones because V5 has only Daunt and Dread Gaze. I made dementation a Nightmare power. I also twisted chimestry into something a bit darker to make it into a Nightmare power.<br /> <br /> I also made Feral Injection an Animalism and Dominate amalgam that lets the user use mental discipline on frenzied vampire with a bonus equal to animalism dots instead of granting the target any bonus die.<br /> <br /> I made Requiem's Lord of the Land discipline into an Animalism and Dominate Amalgam as I thought it fits the Ventrue of VTR quite well.<br /> <br /> I'm planning on converting a few devotions into amalgam as well. Since I plan on letting players buy out discipline power for experience instead of locking them to only five. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">As an eternal homebrewer I\u2019m having fun and I feel like it\u2019s gonna turn out rather balanced at the end. If not\u2026 oh well, that\u2019s what personal erratas are for!</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T16:28:19-07:00","id":1521703,"title":"","content":"It's fun to try to make these powers and it's quite enjoyable to make some level 6 Disciplines into interesting Amalgam powers though I tend to focus on the more subtle and way less flashy powers myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T13:41:49-07:00","id":1521776,"title":"","content":"One of these times I should make a post on some of the Amalgam powers that I came up with and see what ways I can make them better for future use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T09:14:53-07:00","id":1521817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1521776#post1521776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of these times I should make a post on some of the Amalgam powers that I came up with and see what ways I can make them better for future use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell yeah, i'd be interested!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T10:18:30-07:00","id":1521888,"title":"","content":"Good to hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T10:28:40-07:00","id":1521889,"title":"","content":"Here is one Amalgam power I'm fine tuning right now.<br /> <br /> Prophecy (Working title) I'm now calling it Prescience as it focus on possible outcomes instead of it being set in stone<br /> Auspex: 5 Dominate: 4<br /> Cost: 2 Rouse Checks.<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Auspex<br /> Prequistes: Premonition/Compel<br /> <br /> Mostly seen by members of the Malkavian clan, but members of the Tremere &amp; Old Clan Tmiszce have been known to make use this power. Who use this power to gain insight into possible events based on choices that they or other Kindred will make &amp; choose the best possible outcome.<br /> <br /> System: Make an intelligence+auspex roll vs a difficulty depending on how far into a possible future outcome. Roll a difficulty 2 for immediate outcomes in few days/months. Roll Intelligence at difficulty 3 for years and roll a difficulty 4 for decades/centuries.<br /> <br /> Duration: A few minutes for the immediate future, and up to a night for deeper glimpses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  Revamping old work. 09-23-2023, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T10:33:29-07:00","id":1521891,"title":"","content":"I came up with this Amalgam power due to the idea that good help is hard to find and most wise Kindred would know this and try not to needlessly sacafrice their best tools and my main player character uses this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Shared Resilence<br /> Fortitude 2 and Auspex 3<br /> Cost: 1 Rouse Check<br /> Dice Pool: Stamina+ Auspex<br /> Prequistes: Shared Senses/Toughness<br /> System: The Kindred can choose to extend some of their Fortitude powers to ghouls/humans affected by via Auspex. Anyone thus imbued gains additional health levels equal to the fortitude dots of the kindred.<br /> Duration: 1 scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-02-2023, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T10:46:03-07:00","id":1521893,"title":"","content":"This final Amalgam power was a tough one to make as I based it on a high level Dominate power from the Guide To The Camarilla. In essence this power would be largely used by members of the 3rd generation and there direct childer, but anyone old and powerful enough can learn it to keep track of their lineage quietly and gain insights from what they learned, sense final death or get a rough idea where they are in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Blood Scrying<br /> Auspex 5 Obfuscate 3<br /> Cost: 2 Rouse Checks<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Auspex<br /> Prerequistes: Share The Senses<br /> System: Roll resolve at difficulty 2 to target a direct childe of your lineage as per share the senses. The difficulty increases by one for every generation removed is from you.<br /> Duration: 1 scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  Revisions. 09-23-2023, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T19:41:05-07:00","id":1521939,"title":"","content":"Since, once, I was trying to come up with some pre-Indo-European powers; I was studying Finnish folk-lore and came across something like, &quot;the Origin of Fire&quot;, as Finnish folk-magic, required to know the origin of something. I don't know where those notes are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T23:17:10-07:00","id":1521952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1521893#post1521893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This final Amalgam power was a tough one to make as I based it on a high level Dominate power from the Guide To The Camarilla. In essence this power would be largely used by members of the 3rd generation and there direct childer, but anyone old and powerful enough can learn it to keep track of their lineage quietly and gain insights from what they learned, sense final death or get a rough idea where they are in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Blood Scrying<br /> Auspex 5 Obfuscate 3<br /> Cost: 2 Rouse Checks<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Auspex<br /> Prerequistes: Share The Senses<br /> System: Roll resolve at difficulty 3 to target a direct childe of your lineage as per share the senses. The difficulty increases by one for every generation removed is from you.<br /> Duration: 1 scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who thinks that cosanguine relations play a far to small role in this setting this is a power I really like to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T11:12:27-07:00","id":1521991,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the appreciation Gurkal. I love to hear feedback from some of the hard work we all put in our games. Hopefully later I will post more Amalgam powers and get some more feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-03-2023, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T10:26:56-07:00","id":1522099,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Thanks for sharing your power, Lysander! Here\u2019s my feed back.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Prophecy:</b> It seems like the natural progression of premonition. While I personally don\u2019t quite like powers that peer into the future for gameplay reasons, I can see the appeal. If I have one issue with it, is that I fail to see the connection with dominate and compel. Dominate seems to imply control.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I recently made/coonverted a blood Sorcery power for Theban sorcerer for my V5 Requiem adaptation, and I think it could be an interesting Aupex/Dominate amalgam. Feel free to adapt and use it!</span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Malediction of Despair</b></span></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Tradition:</b> Kigan and Theban Sorcery</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">With an ominous incantation, the ritualist weaves a prophecy that shrouds their chosen target in uncertainty and doubt, foretelling a doom and despair.</span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25a0</span></b><b> Cost:</b> One Rouse Check and a point of willpower.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25a0</span> <b>Dice Pools:</b> Charisma + Blood Sorcery vs Resolve + Wits</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25a0</span> <b>System:</b> The user rolls a contest of Charisma + Blood Sorcery vs the Resolve + Wits of a target vampire in line of sight while concentrating for a turn and proclaiming their prophecy. The prophecy can be vague and metaphorical, but if it\u2019s too vague, it there is a risk it never happens. The Prophecy can be no longer than a sentence or two. For example : \u2018\u2019 If you foot into Elysium you shall make a fool of yourself\u2019\u2019 or \u2018\u2019 The next blade that strikes you will strike true\u2019\u2019.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">On a win, if the conditions for the prophecy are met, the victim will suffer a -5 penalty on their next actions in a way that can help making the prophecy come to fruition. On a Critical win, they automatically fail their actions instead. Should they resist your attempt they are immune for the rest of the night. A victim can only be under the effect of one prophecy at a time.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">To be aware that a victim has truly been cursed, they can roll an intelligence + Occult against a difficulty of 5. A victim that\u2019s noticed this power being used before reduce the difficulty by 2.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>For example: </b>If you prophesize \u2018\u2019 The next blade that strikes you will strike true\u2019\u2019, it might give a -5 to a contested combat roll, or to an awareness roll to avoid getting stabbed by surprised. If the prophecy was \u2019\u2019If you foot into Elysium you shall make a fool of yourself\u2019\u2019, the victim might suffer a -5 to the first etiquette roll they might make.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25a0</span> <b>Duration:</b> One lunar month.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Shared Resilience: </b>It might step a bight on Draught of Endurance\u2019s toes, but it is pretty interesting and has its twist. Would the user be able to impart fortitude on a subject they are scrying or it\u2019s supposed to be uniquely reserved to Share the Senses? I think Requiem had a devotion doing something similar combining Fortitude and Dominate.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Blood Scrying: </b>Very thematic, super cool idea, i love it. It reinforces Elder\u2019s mystique and power over their bloodline that\u2019s 100% on brand. Reminds me a bit of blood Sympathy from Requiem, but boosted by Auspex. My only concern is the dice pool. Is it supposed to be Resolve only? Difficulty 3 is pretty hard to get on a single stat roll. </span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T10:36:56-07:00","id":1522100,"title":"","content":"I figured Dominate would fit due to the fact that the user is trying to control the flow of possibilty of information that might overwhelm his or her senses. As for Shared Resilence I viewed it uniquely through Share The Senses power and not through Blood Scrying. As for Blood Scrying I thought Resolve fit the best as for the idea and as for the difficulty You might have a point on the difficulty level and might change that bit. But I didn't want it to be a easy Amalgam power to learn and felt that even potent elders &amp; ancients would have trouble keeping track of there lines due to typical supernatural defenses that they would all have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-05-2023, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T11:11:57-07:00","id":1522107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1522100#post1522100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured Dominate would fit due to the fact that the user is trying to control the flow of possibilty of information that might overwhelm his or her senses</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair Enough. From your description it could also fit as a Fortitude amalgam requiring unswayable mind. However i get the idea of making this a Malkavian amalgam as it's quite literally what they do. I my opinion, the power currently simply read as an Auspex power as foretelling falls entirely within auspex thematic parameters. However, again, i get the idea of making this into an amalgam so it isn't easily available to neonates. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1522100#post1522100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for Shared Resilence I viewed it uniquely through Share The Senses power and not through Blood Scrying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, i see. Yeah that's what i felt like the intent of the amalgam was, however i wasn't too sure has the system text simply mentioned '' ghouls/humans affected by via Auspex. '' <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519182-have-you-ever-spent-the-day-just-creating-new-amalgam-powers-or-disciplines-powers?p=1522100#post1522100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for Blood Scrying I thought Resolve fit the best as for the idea and as for the difficulty You might have a point on the difficulty level and might change that bit. But I didn't want it to be a easy Amalgam power to learn and felt that even potent elders &amp; ancients would have trouble keeping track of there lines due to typical supernatural defenses that they would all have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no i quite agree that this should be an elder power. Might only use with it was that the system text seems to imply that the pool is limited to resolve. Meaning only a vampire with 5 dots of resolve would resonably hit the difficulty 3 threshold and it seems next to impossible to scry beyond their first childe as the difficulty ramps pretty quickly. I guess an elder could use blood surge to add a few dice, but that's starting to get quite pricey with a base cost of two rouse checks. If the intented pool is Resolve + Auspex then difficulty 3 is 100% appropriate. <br /> <br /> As a side note, I think i would personally make this power an Auspex/Blood Sorcery amalgam as i think it fits Tremeres very much, but i'm not sure Blood Sorcery can have amalgams, so Auspex/Obfuscate or Auspex/Dominate also feels appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T10:44:21-07:00","id":1522162,"title":"","content":"I'm not a big user of Blood Sorcery myself and your comment on Fortitude being used instead of Dominate for Prophecy got me thinking about reworking it slightly. But given that is closely tied to the Malkavians and they don't have that as part of there initial spread and I was basing it off a Dark Ages clan book that had Auspex and Dementation as the main powers. Such much to think about.<br /> <br /> My idea with Shared Resilence was that my Malkavian would need to physically to impart this power on his ghouls or freelancers at first, then afterwards he could do it via Share The Senses later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-06-2023, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T17:24:39-07:00","id":1522194,"title":"","content":"I might use Fortitude &amp; Obsfucate as a basis for another Amalgam power when I have worked it out more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}